LOCATION:IMU Whittenberger Auditorium
SUMMARY:Disorder of Discourse Performance
DESCRIPTION:This French-language performance (with English subtitles) bri
 ngs to life Michel Foucault's celebrated 1970 inaugural lecture for which
  no recording survives. The questions it raises for education\, freedom o
 f speech\, and our daily lives feel more urgent than ever. A Théâtre na
 tional Bordeaux Aquitaine production\, the performance at IU Bloomington 
 makes only one of the two U.S. stops during Foucault's centenary year.  P
 erformance\, followed by a discussion with the audience
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  This French-language performance (with 
 English subtitles) brings to life Michel Foucault's celebrated 1970 inaug
 ural lecture for which no recording survives. The questions it raises for
  education\, freedom of speech\, and our daily lives feel more urgent tha
 n ever. A Théâtre national Bordeaux Aquitaine production\, the performa
 nce at IU Bloomington makes only one of the two U.S. stops during Foucaul
 t's centenary year.</p><p>  Performance\, followed by a discussion with t
 he audience</p>
