SUMMARY:Renaissance Studies Graduate Student Roundtable
DESCRIPTION:Please save the date for the 18th roundtable featuring the ex
 citing work of advanced graduate students from a wide variety of discipli
 nes\, exploring issues of general interest to scholars of Renaissance and
  early modern studies. The roundtable will begin at 4 pm with brief prese
 ntations by each panelist\, followed by Q&amp\;A\, before we continue the
  exchange at the reception. The panelists are:Nathaniel Rudavsky-Brody (C
 omparative Literature)\, "Epic Continuities from Ariosto to Milton: Liter
 ature\, Myth\, or Folklore?"  Dissertation title: Song Forms and the Ends
  of VerseLeanna York (Musicology)\, "'A Lasting Monument': Music in the E
 nglish Memory."  Dissertation title: Memory\, Motion\, and Sense in Renai
 ssance English Theories of MusicYuqi Sun (History and Philosophy of Scien
 ce and Medicine)\, "Richard Wentworth\, a Tudor Mathematician between Ven
 ice and England."  Dissertation title: TBA  This will be a great chance t
 o meet faculty and graduate students working in other disciplines.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p class="p1">  Please save the date for the
  18th roundtable featuring the exciting work of advanced graduate student
 s from a wide variety of disciplines\, exploring issues of general intere
 st to scholars of Renaissance and early modern studies. The roundtable wi
 ll begin at 4 pm with brief presentations by each panelist\, followed by 
 Q&amp\;A\, before we continue the exchange at the reception. The panelist
 s are:</p><p class="p1"><strong>Nathaniel Rudavsky-Brody</strong> (Compar
 ative Literature)\, "Epic Continuities from Ariosto to Milton: Literature
 \, Myth\, or Folklore?"<br />  Dissertation title: Song Forms and the End
 s of Verse</p><p class="p1"><strong>Leanna York</strong> (Musicology)\, "
 'A Lasting Monument': Music in the English Memory."<br />  Dissertation t
 itle: Memory\, Motion\, and Sense in Renaissance English Theories of Musi
 c</p><p class="p1"><strong>Yuqi Sun</strong> (History and Philosophy of S
 cience and Medicine)\, "Richard Wentworth\, a Tudor Mathematician between
  Venice and England."<br />  Dissertation title: TBA</p><p class="p1">  T
 his will be a great chance to meet faculty and graduate students working 
 in other disciplines.</p>
